  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.",
      "oracle_id": "049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Playing a land is not casting a spell, so playing a land will not trigger this card.",
      "oracle_id": "11eb31d9-cbcb-4ec5-abab-dfa646addbba",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A planeswalker with indestructible still loses loyalty counters as it's dealt damage and will still be put into its owner's graveyard if its loyalty reaches 0.",
      "oracle_id": "24882fa2-3fe9-4c1b-aa3d-0e6488b9db27",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The set of permanents affected by Heroic Intervention is determined as the spell resolves. Permanents you begin to control later in the turn won't gain hexproof and indestructible.",
      "oracle_id": "24882fa2-3fe9-4c1b-aa3d-0e6488b9db27",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A battle with indestructible still loses defense counters as it's dealt damage. If it's a Siege, it will still be exiled when the last defense counter is removed from it, and its controller may still cast it transformed without paying its mana cost.",
      "oracle_id": "24882fa2-3fe9-4c1b-aa3d-0e6488b9db27",
      "published_at": "2023-07-28",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The spell will be countered even if Lunar Force can\u2019t be sacrificed, most likely because it has already left the battlefield. Casting a spell in response to an opponent\u2019s Lunar Force\u2019s triggered ability is generally a bad idea.",
      "oracle_id": "31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799",
      "published_at": "2016-07-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can\u2019t choose not to sacrifice Lunar Force.",
      "oracle_id": "31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799",
      "published_at": "2016-07-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You sacrifice Lunar Force even if the spell\u2019s already been countered, perhaps by the ability of another Lunar Force, or if the spell can\u2019t be countered.",
      "oracle_id": "31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799",
      "published_at": "2016-07-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Triggers when you announce a creature spell, and will resolve before that creature is put onto the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "4344abeb-47ab-4638-b50f-dd502f14c1af",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2004-12-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\"."
    },
    {
      "comment": "A \u201ccreature spell\u201d is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.",
      "oracle_id": "6e48981b-8971-4b7c-ae05-29c7e4091a05",
      "published_at": "2008-04-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the permanent was an Aura or an Equipment, it becomes unattached from whatever it was attached to.",
      "oracle_id": "7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594",
      "published_at": "2014-11-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The enchanted permanent loses any card types, subtypes, and colors it previously had. It keeps any supertypes it had and its name remains unchanged. It gains \u201c{T}: Add {G}\u201d and loses all other abilities from its rules text. It will still have any abilities it gained from other effects.",
      "oracle_id": "7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594",
      "published_at": "2014-11-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a spell, the spell goes on the stack, then Illusory Demon\u2019s triggered ability goes on the stack on top of it. The triggered ability will resolve (and you\u2019ll sacrifice Illusory Demon) before the spell resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "91d0a557-7a80-46d5-b823-392a84a6be44",
      "published_at": "2009-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the card returns to the battlefield, it will be a new object with no connection to the card that was exiled. Auras attached to the exiled creature will be put into their owners' graveyards. Any Equipment will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creature will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.",
      "oracle_id": "c6cd6934-b661-455a-8de5-ceb920664bbe",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature is sacrificed as a cost to cast a spell or activate an ability, Mortician Beetle\u2019s ability resolves before that spell or ability.",
      "oracle_id": "dc5c4a38-a415-466a-a7ea-dc04eee7f691",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Mortician Beetle\u2019s ability triggers whenever any player, including you, sacrifices a creature because some other spell, ability, or cost instructed the player to do so. Mortician Beetle itself doesn\u2019t allow you to sacrifice any creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "dc5c4a38-a415-466a-a7ea-dc04eee7f691",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability triggers when the creature spell is cast, and it is put on the stack before any responses can be cast or activated. This ability will resolve before that creature enters.",
      "oracle_id": "fae1d5d9-a50e-423e-8692-3e41f39df081",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A \"creature spell\" is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.",
      "oracle_id": "fae1d5d9-a50e-423e-8692-3e41f39df081",
      "published_at": "2008-04-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Buyback causes a spell to go to your hand instead of your graveyard, so using Buyback will avoid triggering this card to be sacrificed.",
      "oracle_id": "fbf7a7f4-9915-4a53-84b3-e55e9f487323",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Discarding does trigger this.",
      "oracle_id": "fbf7a7f4-9915-4a53-84b3-e55e9f487323",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
